        }
      ],
      "completion": "partial",
      "explanation": "HO2 was triggered by medication confusion and the doctor partially clarified that glycyrrhizin was liver-related and pancreatic enzyme was digestive. It is not complete because the doctor did not clearly tie a misconception correction to teach-back or explicitly correct any belief that these medicines treat or dissolve gallstones.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
